# Innate Domain: importing a Shikigami library.
#
# `Innate Domain: lib/shapes` loads examples/lib/shapes.domain before this
# program, so its operations are callable by name — exactly like the prelude's.
# Imports are declarations, not pipeline steps, so the line can sit anywhere;
# by convention it goes at the top.
#
# Libraries cost nothing at runtime: a Shikigami is inlined at its call site,
# so `Biggest` fuses into a quickselect just as if it had been written here.
# Run with --explain to watch that happen through the import.
#
#   domain examples/18_innate_domain.domain
#   Expected output: 28
Innate Domain: lib/shapes
Cursed Energy: 18_innate_domain.input
Shikigami: Lines
Shikigami: All Ints
Shikigami: Biggest
    n: 3
Reveal: stdout
